Here is a complete rewrite of the text using different phrasing and structure while preserving all the original details:

An apparatus for magnetic gearing is built from five key components: 

* A round primary rotor featuring a ring of multiple alternating magnetic pole pairs along its outer edge;
* A primary field-adjusting frame containing a circular arrangement of magnetic elements that alter the spatial distribution of the magnetic field emitted by the primary rotor;
* A round secondary rotor positioned along virtually the same central axis as the primary rotor, which similarly carries a ring of alternating pole pairs;
* A secondary field-adjusting frame holding a circular set of magnetic elements designed to alter the spatial distribution of the secondary rotor's magnetic field; and
* A round intermediate rotor situated in the gap between the two field-adjusting frames, which establishes a magnetic connection between the primary and secondary rotors through these two intervening frames.

