Here is an independent claim written in standard USPTO/WIPO patent formatting:

1. A dual-rotor magnetic gear device, comprising:

	a first rotor rotatable about a central axis and comprising a first plurality of magnetic poles configured to generate a first magnetic field;

	a second rotor rotatable about the central axis and comprising a second plurality of magnetic poles configured to generate a second magnetic field;

	a central linking rotor rotatably supported about the central axis and positioned operatively between the first rotor and the second rotor, the central linking rotor comprising a third plurality of magnetic elements;

	a first magnetic-field-modulating yoke disposed within a first air gap defined between the first rotor and the central linking rotor, the first magnetic-field-modulating yoke comprising a first plurality of spaced-apart ferromagnetic pole pieces configured to modulate the first magnetic field; and

	a second magnetic-field-modulating yoke disposed within a second air gap defined between the central linking rotor and the second rotor, the second magnetic-field-modulating yoke comprising a second plurality of spaced-apart ferromagnetic pole pieces configured to modulate the second magnetic field;

	wherein rotation of the first rotor induces rotation of the central linking rotor via modulated magnetic flux passing through the first magnetic-field-modulating yoke, and wherein rotation of the central linking rotor induces rotation of the second rotor via modulated magnetic flux passing through the second magnetic-field-modulating yoke, thereby transmitting torque between the first rotor and the second rotor at a predetermined gear ratio.

Here is a draft of an independent patent claim based on your requirements:

1. A magnetic gear device comprises:

  a first discoid rotor rotatably arranged about a central axis of rotation and carrying a first plurality of magnetic poles arranged circumferentially thereon;

  a second discoid rotor rotatably arranged about the central axis of rotation, coaxial with the first discoid rotor, and carrying a second plurality of magnetic poles arranged circumferentially thereon;

  a discoid linking rotor coaxial with the central axis of rotation and positioned axially between the first discoid rotor and the second discoid rotor, the discoid linking rotor comprising a third plurality of magnetic elements;

  a first magnetic-field-modulating yoke positioned axially between the first discoid rotor and the discoid linking rotor, the first magnetic-field-modulating yoke comprising a plurality of first soft-magnetic pole pieces spaced apart to modulate a magnetic field between the first discoid rotor and the discoid linking rotor; and

  a second magnetic-field-modulating yoke positioned axially between the second discoid rotor and the discoid linking rotor, the second magnetic-field-modulating yoke comprising a plurality of second soft-magnetic pole pieces spaced apart to modulate a magnetic field between the second discoid rotor and the discoid linking rotor,

  wherein rotation of the first discoid rotor drives rotation of the second discoid rotor via magnetic coupling extended through the first magnetic-field-modulating yoke, the discoid linking rotor, and the second magnetic-field-modulating yoke.
